From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaughanb <brenden.vaughan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:39:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Send one-shot movement flags to every receiver of a tick

The server send loops write each entity once per receiver, and
WriteServerState and CreateMovementData cleared the jump, dash, teleport
and still-move flags inside that write, so only the first player written
in a tick received them. An owner written after another player never got
its own IsTeleport and never confirmed it, so a same-map respawn in view
of an earlier-joined player waited forever in WaitClientTeleportConfirm.

The writes now only read the flags. Handlers with one-shot flags
implement the new IEntityMovementServerStateFlags, and both send loops
consume them once per tick, after the last player, through
EntityMovementServerStateFlagsPass: a handler is recorded after each
successful write, and a pass that throws leaves its flags for the next
tick. NavMeshEntityMovement's consume also clears _sendingDash, which a
server never cleared: after one dash every state carried IsDash and was
sent reliably.

OnTeleport now restarts interpolation at the destination, as the snap in
ReadServerStateAtClient does. Without it a remote copy was drawn back to
its last pre-teleport state on the next frame, and the server checked
(and, while the character was dead, clamped) the owner's teleport
confirmation against that stale state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
